version: 1.0.0
license: MIT
date-released: 2026-09-26
abstract: >-
  Reproducibility package for the Ising block-dynamics example in
  Rapid mixing of Gibbs samplers via quantum Dobrushin–Shlosman conditions.
  Exhaustive transfer-matrix computations with explicit roundoff bounds certify
  positive square-block Dobrushin–Shlosman margins at beta J = 0.35 and 0.36,
  where the single-site condition fails. Includes source code, certified data,
  independent verification, figures, and conservative perturbation-window calculations.
keywords:
  - Ising model
  - block dynamics
  - Dobrushin–Shlosman condition
  - rapid mixing
  - reproducible numerics
  - quantum Gibbs sampling
